implementationPlan.description:
Verification, run once. From your worktree root, run exactly the executionContract checkRef, which is byte-identical to /mnt/d/moe-scratch/7e735953-plan/gate.sh; check it first with `cd /mnt/d/moe-scratch/7e735953-plan && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`. Submit the gate's fresh output as moe.complete_task verification.
The gate:
1. clones your HEAD into mktemp, outside the shared checkout;
2. overlays your 3 working-tree files;
3. runs npm ci and `npx tsc --noEmit -p .`;
4. runs vitest on parkedUnlandedLanding, finalizeAttempt, finalizingCloseRetry, parkedReview.guard and attemptHandback.
The architect's run with the prototype gave 5 files and 127 tests passing. DoD 2 requires finalizeAttempt.test.ts and finalizingCloseRetry.test.ts to pass with no edits to those files.
Never run npm ci, npm test or a build in /mnt/d/projexts/moes or in your worktree (global rail 1). For any scratch prototyping, use absolute destination paths inside `( set -e; ... )` (mem:gotcha-scratch-clone-relative-cp-falls-through).
